  designNotes: 'Beat 11: the exam. Default is 6 rifle + 1 sniper + 1 rocket so the
    player sorts fragile-and-dangerous from tough-and-slow with the matching guns.
    The chart offers a helicopter here OR a focus-fire
    test; HELI_ENABLED is false for camera-load reasons that are a real problem rather
    than a stale flag, so this is the skill version. Rocket troopers and heavies
    on one post: everything is either fragile-and-dangerous or tough-and-slow, and
    the player has to sort them under a turn limit of their own patience. Was a 6v6
    stub with no payout that broke the locked 7-30 roster scale. Wave added 2026-08-07
    (Tier 1.2 schedule). This was the only stage-2 level the audit called NO MECHANIC,
    and the beat chart names its own fallback - "else elite push" - so the push is
    delivered as a TELEGRAPHED wave rather than as three more bodies in the opening
    formation. Three heavies on turn 4, warned from turn 2, is what turns the focus-fire
    exam into a timed one: sort the rockets from the heavies BEFORE the reinforcement
    lands, or sort a bigger problem afterwards. The lead is 2 to match L10, so the
    campaign teaches one clock, not two. Ground units at x 8, NOT garrisoned: the
    beach post is already at 288-capacity limits and a wave that had to be shot off
    a deck would spend siege damage the squad does not have. Waves are enemy-side
    only, so the star math (player-roster based) is untouched. WAVE MOVED 2026-08-12, anchorX 8 -> 9: at 8 the first of its three heavies stood 0.71 INSIDE GarrisonPost''s collision box - unhittable except by a near-vertical plunge (rule 8, which until that day never looked at mid-battle arrivals). At 9 the nearest man clears the box edge (7.88) by 0.28 and the deepest sits at 91% power from the front rank, 99% from the back - in reach, and the beat is unchanged: the elite push still lands BEHIND the post, two turns after its warning. An earlier attempt moved the wave in front of the post at anchorX 0 on the belief that there was no room behind it; that belief came from a hand-rolled reach estimate (x - backRank > 20.25) which ignores dy and the launch envelope, and BalanceAudit.ReachRule - the only implementation that counts - disagreed with it. Do not re-derive reach; ask ReachRule. WAVE 2026-08-17: Rob, they sit to the right of the post and are very hard to hit. Moved to the FRONT (anchorX 3, clear of the box at 4.13) with advancePerTurn 1.2. Heavies have no melee, so they walk up and hold as a firing line. Timed exam stays.'
